#{[17592186403048 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 2x+6 \\\\ y\\le 5\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403048 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403048 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cc2ec7bb-7f05-5512-a12e-01138a6573c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403049 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}y>2x+6 \\\\ y<5\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403049 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403049 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "17af44de-3d26-5293-8028-23cd473e2e0b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403050 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}y>2x+6 \\\\ y>5\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403050 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403050 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b7ebc338-a51c-54a2-9008-89b303d45e94" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404461 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404461 #edb/ref 1069 "q-90054" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404461 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404461 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/b8/b8c1d5902a76a68e5f8358d4c3668e1be184ec7241184df4ff1363d41995f3aa.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404461 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "262609c0-5557-5285-b43c-f82fdb8825a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404461 #edb/ref 1074 "Consider the line $x+y=3.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=-x+3.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\"  inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>-x+3,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx+y>3.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=2x.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict.  Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>2x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y>3 \\\\ y>2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404462 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404462 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404462 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404462 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404462 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404462 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404462 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404462 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186404467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404462 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8c5be21f-60e7-597b-83dc-3c20339aa469" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404463 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}x+y<3 \\\\ y>2x\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404463 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404463 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c7c2a5d4-298c-5631-a9d7-aba5b729e118" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404464 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}x+y\\le 3 \\\\ y\\ge 2x\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404464 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404464 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "01bc8bf9-9741-5be3-bf6c-963968a707d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404465 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}x+y>3 \\\\ y<2x\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404465 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404465 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "da29e297-529e-5fe2-b38a-d2962daba4be" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404466 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}x+y<3 \\\\ y<2x\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404466 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404466 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2f5ca256-25d0-5c51-b2d0-61bafb216142" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404467 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}x+y>3 \\\\ y>2x\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404467 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404467 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "57ca1c9c-b7c8-5c26-8e55-f2e99026a45b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404468 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404469 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404468 #edb/ref 1069 "q-90323" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404468 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404468 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/e8/e863789ff989ee1cb3d3fe6c22fe0d4daa1dac76d6fbfbebdad801006ca4c969.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404468 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "66b0d8c5-2487-53cc-b840-b06edcc12d56" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404468 #edb/ref 1074 "Consider the line $y=4x+3.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<4x+3.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{4}x-2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>\\frac{1}{4}x-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y<4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404469 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404470 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404469 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404471 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404469 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404469 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404469 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404469 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404469 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404469 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186404471 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404469 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "94914b35-e16f-5398-9a50-4baddb153e6e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404470 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404470 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404470 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "57e3339b-5c2d-5e02-8e56-922ef2cb88bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404471 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}y<4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404471 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404471 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b2167803-87c2-5c4e-aa85-d576aac9cc32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404472 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}y>4x+3 \\\\ y\\ge \\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404472 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404472 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aa93daa1-24f9-58db-9545-6bf0487628c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404473 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}y>4x+3 \\\\ y<\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404473 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404473 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ecf061e8-e3ee-5abf-a78a-299067a79064" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404474 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}y>4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404474 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404474 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6051d13a-7c7c-5804-88c5-53711a5cb6ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404475 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404475 #edb/ref 1069 "q-90327" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404475 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404475 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/76/762e53967ddb3ccddfa1c9b7a2aa303d66fc1b761c9be8f409c0b91ecb0201de.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities represents the shaded region shown in the graph above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404475 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3e5e2c49-2afd-5324-972b-43974f8bfdd9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404475 #edb/ref 1074 "Consider the line $y=x+2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le x+2.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=-x+2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>-x+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y>-x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404476 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404476 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404476 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404479 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404476 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404480 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404476 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404481 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404476 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404476 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404476 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186404479 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404476 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f86fe5f2-d23c-5598-bb24-07f9f597ec1a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404477 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+2\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404477 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 1759218604549